   "joint": "J7 (last wrist rotation joint), both arms",
   "observation": "rotates continuously through 360 deg, any number of turns (no mechanical stop)",
   "consistent_with_data": "J7 crosses_pm180=true on both arms, single-step jumps of about 179-180 deg",
   "implications": [
    "the reported value is single-turn in [-180, 180); turn count is lost and the value jumps by about 360 deg at each wrap",
    "the vendor SDK keeps the previous value when one step changes by >= 180 deg, so a wrap can freeze the reading near +-180 until the joint returns past the opposite half",
    "a joint-copy mapping to AR5 J7 (+-60 deg) cannot represent it; a pose-based mapping should treat J7 modulo 360 deg"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "notes": [
  "Observed ranges are what the operator reached in this session; true mechanical limits may be slightly wider.",
  "crosses_pm180=true: the joint turned past +-180 deg, so the encoder value wrapped (single-step jumps near 360 deg); its real range exceeds what [-180, 180) can show directly.",
  "With the original joint-copy mapping only J5 stays inside the AR5 range; J4/J6/J7 ranges are wider on LinkerTA, and the J1-J3 mapping constants shift the LinkerTA ranges past the AR5 ends."
